Z||000000||Master_Sushi||08-01-2000||11:53 AM||||Well....<BR>The original rubber on my 88 fiero is starting to get really bad. The wheels are starting to lose about a pound every few days <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">, and are getting towards bald. I am thinking about just getting some new tires, on the stock 14-inch rins are P185 75R14. If I go with just getting new tires I would like to get something a little wider and sportier, but without throwing off the Speedo. I was wondering what you guys would recommend. But also the rims are starting to get a little worn, the clearcoat is chipping and I really don't want to go through the hassle of repairing them. So I need some help here, what would you guys (and gals  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">) do? Also I'm really not looking to spend a "lot" of money.<BR>Thanks allot! and sorry for the long post.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Monkeyman||08-01-2000||03:11 PM||||Seems to me that the stock size would either be:<P>205/60/14 or<P>215/60/14||||reg||1
Z||000002||Master_Sushi||08-01-2000||03:39 PM||||Hmmmm... <P>They must not be orignal then, they sure seem like it though.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Master_Sushi||08-01-2000||03:40 PM||||Hmmmm... <P>They must not be orignal then, they sure seem like it though.||||reg||1
Z||000004||CHUCKVH||08-02-2000||01:33 AM||||According to the door sticker on my 88 coupe, the 185/75-14 is the original tire size.  I am currently running 215/60-14s on the stock rim, but it seems to have thrown my speedo off by close to 5 mph.  A 195/70-14 is a pretty close match diameter-wise, with a little extra width.  Can somebody tell me what the stock tire size was for 15x7 GT wheels?||||reg||1
Z||000005||nivlek68||08-02-2000||08:01 AM||||my door sticker says 195/70R14, and it also has P195/70R15<BR>the P195/70R14 is 24.80 in dia.<BR>    P215/60R14    24.17<BR>    P205/60R14    23.70||||reg||1
Z||000006||Carrolles||08-02-2000||08:06 AM||||Do a search for Speedometer.  Some time back someone posted info about a small black box that wires into the speedometer circuit and allows you to adjust the readout for your tire size.||||reg||1
Z||000007||2birds||08-02-2000||04:45 PM||||15" GT wheels of all years had 205/60/15 in front and 215/60/15 in back.  The 88's had different front wheels, slightly narrower (I think), and with no dish, but the 86-87 were the same (15X7) front and rear.  I run 215/60 in front and 225/60 in back on my 86 GT, with no problems.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Xtreme Fiero's||08-02-2000||04:54 PM||||My 84 se has 87 black GT rims w/ 225/50/Z15 rubber and my speedometer is right ive has it checked by the local police.||||reg||1
Z||000009||nivlek68||08-03-2000||10:14 AM||||the over all diameter is the only thing that will miss up the speedometer.<BR>P195/50R15 is 22.72 in dia.<BR>P195/60R15 is 24.21 ""<BR>P205/50R15 is 23.11 ""<BR>P205/55R16 is 24.88 ""<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000010||Master_Sushi||08-03-2000||11:38 AM||||Ok, I kind of like the idea Xtreme Fiero's and 2birds pointed out. I think it would look good to get some stock GT wheels with 205/60/15 front and 215/60/15 rear. It would almost give my coupe a formula look  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">. <BR>Anyone know where to get 4 gt diamond spokes in good shape for a reasonable price? <P>Thanks all!||||reg||1
